- **Talk says:** everything with a value under, say, 10 is close to the best path, but not necessarily on it [[t:261-262]].
- **Demo:** culls at 15, so a band of floor survives beyond the hot path it shows [[c20:131-154]].
- **The route:** ours is a shortest path; the talk’s A* route [can be longer](#exit-faithfulness). Each side’s hot path follows its own route [[own]].

## Step-through
@@steps limit=4

## Controls
@@control radius
Tiles fewer than this many steps from the route are the hot path [[c20:131-145]]. The lab’s walk also keeps its caches at least this far from the route [[own]].
@@control cull
Tiles this many steps or more from the route become wall [[c20:147-154]]. At 0, nothing is culled [[own]].

## Measured traits
@@measured

- **Cull at 15:** keeps about half the floor. Floor share {{c20.floor_share.median}} at the median, vs {{c18.floor_share.median}} before it; the route is the same {{c20.path.median}} steps [[run:c20.floor_share.median c18.floor_share.median c20.path.median]].
- **Talk says:** for a less branchy game. It removes the parts of the map that are irrelevant, so the player isn’t forced through winding labyrinths with no purpose [[t:263-266]].

